{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789750088,"nonce":"BdxU7fdv5zXD5Dfgk9gUuw1WhDU=","title":"Native plugins on the shared ABI","message":"Phase 4 of the plan: native access for every hosted language is the\nplugin ABI only, and a spoke sees the descriptors the driver grants.\ncaribou_abi has the descriptor table (PluginInfo, SymbolDesc, TypeTag,\nthe two exported symbols) and nothing loads one.\n\nDesign:\n- A plugin is a dynamic library exporting `caribou_abi_version` and\n  `caribou_plugin_entry`. A new stable crate, caribou-plugin, loads one\n  (libloading), refuses another ABI version, and reads its table.\n- Each plugin is a language of its own to the world: the plugin adapter\n  registers one LangId per plugin, named after it, so every plugin has\n  a namespace with no configuration, and `import \"math:Math\" for Math`\n  in Wren or `import math.Math` in Haxe reach it as they reach any\n  language's class.\n- The table publishes to the registry as interfaces: one module per\n  class, named after the class, with the symbols of that class as\n  methods; free functions are the statics of a class named after the\n  plugin. Every target is Callable::Typed with an hl_type HFUN built\n  from the TypeTags, and the plugin's language has a typed dispatcher\n  over ash_native_call, so a call from any language marshals scalars\n  by kind and boxes nothing.\n- The driver loads the plugins in `plugins/` beside the program at\n  open (the project's layout is the configuration), and a bundle's\n  NativeLib sections later.\n\nIncrements: 1. the crate, the adapter, scalar and DYN parameters, a\ntest plugin in the workspace, Wren reaching it, the driver's\ndiscovery. 2. Haxe at build time: the macro describes a plugin\n(`caribou describe` on the library) and emits its externs. 3. plugin\nobjects (TypeTag::OBJ): a native payload held by a core cell through\n`unwrap_native`, with a finalizer. 4. NativeLib sections in the bundle,\nper target. 5. wren_lift's own plugins (wlift_abi) on this ABI, on its\ntracker.","files":null}]}